  "explicit_non_claims": [
    "This evaluator is not a Linux kernel event source, path manager, packet scheduler or route control loop.",
    "Allocated rate is a planning output and is not measured goodput or successful application delivery.",
    "Event source SHA-256 is syntax checked and echoed; this module does not cryptographically authenticate the event source.",
    "Capacity inventory signatures and issuer authority are verified by a separate trust boundary.",
    "The evaluator does not infer hidden topology or discover shared capacity dependencies.",
    "Events not yet observed or effective at a decision tick cannot influence that tick.",
    "A deferred event is not treated as a path failure or as available capacity.",
    "Service-floor recovery in this evaluator is allocation restoration, not measured first-useful-byte time.",
    "RTT, loss, queue delay, reinjection and packet reordering require an external matched namespace or hardware transport experiment.",
    "No field, carrier, satellite or public-radio experiment is performed by this module.",
    "A passing single replay is not programme-level statistical qualification."
  ]
